UID:26254-1787769000-1787778000@houstonheights.org
SUMMARY:Heights Garden Club Presents: Angel Wing Arts brings this Bee Watering Station Craft to the Heights Garden Club
DESCRIPTION:AUGUST 26th at 6:30pm\, join us at the Heights Fire Station \nCarolyn\, of Angel Wing Arts\, (Instagram @cacoatesart or @anglewingarts) and one of our own\, will lead this workshop. Carolyn has been active in the arts for over 30 years\, from faux finishes to murals to art pieces. She has worked with clients and their art needs\, and her work itself is whimsical and fun. Please join us on August 26\, at our favorite spot to mingle\, the historic Heights Fire station on 12th and Yale streets. There will be a demo\, and plenty of inspiration to kick off your creativity!! \nEach participant will construct two bee watering stations from clay pots and saucers and then decorate them with paints and pens\, as seen in the photo. Let’s help our bees and butterflies in this heat by providing them a safe place to get a drink that YOU are providing with your cute\, personalized vessel. \nReserve your spot through Sign-Up Genius so we have an accurate headcount and can make sure we have the right amount of supplies on hand. But hurry\, there is only room for 25 guests and the deadline to sign up is August 19th. $20 cash per person\, ages 12 and up\, to be paid at the door. Please\, no unaccompanied minors. Doors opens at 6:30pm\, Class is 7-9pm. Please arrive early so that instruction can begin on time. \nWater and some light refreshments will be provided\, but please consider bringing a snack to share\, if you are so inclined. You may bring your own adult beverages if you wish. \n 
URL:https://houstonheights.org/event/heights-garden-club-presents/
LOCATION:Houston Heights City Hall & Fire Station\, 107 W. 12th Street\, Houston\, TX\, 77008\, United States
CATEGORIES:Heights Garden Club
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://houstonheights.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/CE80E614CB2502B3AA564CB4359A4921_0.webp
END:VEVENT
